## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to diagnose subtle cross-region TLS/QUIC interactions during certificate rotation, a realistic pain point in modern multi-region deployments.

## Key Concepts
- TLS certificate rotation impact on handshake latency
- QUIC 1-RTT vs 0-RTT and ticket refresh timing
- L7 load balancer session migration costs
- DNS TTL effects on cross-region path selection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: measure handshake latency around rotation events
async function measureHandshake(region){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  await tlsHandshake(region);
  const t1 = performance.now();
  return t1 - t0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate rotation-aware measurements across regions?
- Which metrics indicate rotation-induced stalls versus LB migration delays?

